  "question": {
    "text": "A train is moving with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> on rails which are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> apart. To negotiate a curve radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, the height by which the outer rail should be raised with respect to the inner rail is (Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>):",
    "image": null
  },
